			"type": "text",
			"text": "Rhenonema eifeliense is a species of holonematid placoderm known from the town of Gerolstein in the Rhineland of Germany. Originally named as a species of Dinichthys, then a species of Holonema, it is only known from a few isolated dorsal plates. However, from these plates we can tell that the animal would have had a massive dorsal crest at least 24 centimeters in length. The animal is estimated to grow to around 2 meters in length."
